; A NON-LAST statement that is only a value does nothing, and since the
; assignment is `target := value` there is a short way to one: `a: 42` -- the
; old `set a: 42` without its keyword -- is the two statements `a` and `42`
; (the colon separates). It compiled at rc 0 and left `a` as it was; a lost
; `set` of that kind sat in tscaly's printer (`written: true`). Planner.
; report_value_statement#, 2026-10-04.
; xfail: this statement is only a value and does nothing

var a 1
a: 42
if a = 42
    print "PASS"
